  "attack_progression": [
    {"step": 1, "tactic": "Reconnaissance / Gather Victim Org Information — Identify Roles", "technique": "T1591.004", "what_happened": "At 2027-09-14 09:02:11 CEST, Suricata logged the start of a targeted, aggressive web crawl with data.srcip=45.83.12.7 against the corporate HR/careers web application at data.dstip=10.108.57.198. The crawl was NOT a broad directory brute-force — it walked a very specific set of org-structure URLs: /team, /our-team, /leadership, /executives, /management, /board, /board-of-directors, /directors, /people, /staff, /ceo, /cfo, /cto, /ciso, /cio, /coo, /executive-team, /c-suite, /managing-director. Each request rotated through 3 desktop browser User-Agent strings (macOS Safari, Windows Chrome, Windows Firefox) to blunt naive UA-based rate limiting, with ~16 second pacing between requests. This URL set has a single coherent intent: enumerate decision-makers, reporting lines and the leadership org chart of the target company.", "chain_reason": "Suricata signature 'ET SCAN Aggressive Web Crawl' fired with data.srcip=45.83.12.7 against data.dstip=10.108.57.198, with data.url values matching the leadership/exec page set and data.http.user_agent rotating across 3 strings. rule.mitre.id T1591.004 (Gather Victim Org Information: Identify Roles) was attached by the rule.", "first_seen": "2027-09-14T09:02:11+0200"},
    {"step": 2, "tactic": "Reconnaissance / Gather Victim Org Information — Business Relationships & Tempo", "technique": "T1591.003", "what_happened": "At ~09:11 CEST, after a brief inter-phase pause, the same data.srcip=45.83.12.7 shifted to careers/job-listing enumeration: /careers, /jobs, /job-openings, /open-positions, /careers/finance, /careers/it, /careers/security, /careers/hr, /jobs/filter?dept=finance, /jobs/filter?dept=engineering, /jobs/filter?dept=security, /api/jobs, /api/careers, /api/v1/positions. Job postings are intelligence gold — they leak internal team names, the tool stack (Salesforce, SAP, Workday, Okta, CyberArk), headcount, and 'reports to [VP/Director]' reporting lines. The crawl then walked business-tempo URLs: /investor-relations, /earnings, /quarterly-results, /annual-report, /events, /calendar, /news?year=2025&month=12, /press?year=2026&q=1 — used to infer the fiscal calendar and month-end deadlines for timing a future BEC/fraud attack. Same ~20-22s pacing, same rotating User-Agents.", "chain_reason": "Continuation of the same Suricata 'ET SCAN Aggressive Web Crawl' alert stream from data.srcip=45.83.12.7 against data.dstip=10.108.57.198, data.url values shifting from leadership pages to careers/job and investor/events pages. rule.mitre.id T1591.003 (Gather Victim Org Information: Identify Business Tempo) attached.", "first_seen": "2027-09-14T09:11:30+0200"},
    {"step": 3, "tactic": "Reconnaissance / Gather Victim Org Information — Per-person Profile Enumeration", "technique": "T1591.004", "what_happened": "At ~09:24 CEST the same data.srcip=45.83.12.7 began directly probing person-specific profile API endpoints using role slugs and standard corporate username formats discovered in Step 1: /api/users/ceo, /api/users/cfo, /api/users/cto, /api/users/ciso, /api/profiles/vp-finance, /api/profiles/director-it, /api/v1/employees/head-security, /team/john.smith, /team/alice.jones, /people/david.miller, /people/laura.taylor, /api/users/sarah.chen, /api/users/marc.dupont. Several of these returned HTTP 200 with JSON bodies, indicating the API exposes role, title, department, email and manager fields per person without authentication — a direct identity-information leak that feeds straight into a phishing/BEC target list.", "chain_reason": "Same Suricata 'ET SCAN Aggressive Web Crawl' stream, data.srcip=45.83.12.7, data.url values matching /api/users/*, /api/profiles/*, /api/v1/employees/*, /team/* and /people/* slug patterns. rule.mitre.id T1591.004 (Identify Roles) reattached; some events also tagged with the web flood correlation rule.", "first_seen": "2027-09-14T09:24:05+0200"},
    {"step": 4, "tactic": "Reconnaissance / Cumulative Volume", "technique": "T1591.004", "what_happened": "Across the 09:02-09:33 window (~31 minutes), Wazuh aggregated the per-request Suricata crawl alerts plus Wazuh rule 31101 (web flood / excessive 404 and 200 requests from a single external source) into one correlated incident: ~64 distinct alerts with data.srcip=45.83.12.7 against data.dstip=10.108.57.198. The single-external-source + coherent org-recon URL set + User-Agent rotation + polite ~16-22s pacing is the canonical org-information reconnaissance fingerprint that MITRE T1591 (Gather Victim Org Information) describes — specifically the .003 (Business Tempo) and .004 (Identify Roles) sub-techniques.", "chain_reason": "Wazuh correlation rule 'Web crawl + flood from single external source against web application' fired on aggregate count of Suricata 'ET SCAN Aggressive Web Crawl' + rule 31101 events sharing data.srcip=45.83.12.7 within a 1-hour window. The MITRE mapping T1591.003 / T1591.004 was attached automatically by the rule.", "first_seen": "2027-09-14T09:33:00+0200"}
  ],
